<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Greek Civil War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1946">1946</a>–<a href="/years/1949">1949</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Greek Civil War was fought from 1946 to 1949 between the government army, supported by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and then the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, and the communist-led Democratic Army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. It grew out of conflict between the resistance movement EAM-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greek-peoples-liberation-army">ELAS</a> and the returning government in 1944. Tens of thousands died before the communists were defeated in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grammos">Grammos</a> and Vitsi mountains in 1949, leaving deep divisions.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/greek-civil-war.jpg" alt="Greek Civil War" width="320" height="176" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vladina_edinica,_Gradjanska_vojna_vo_Grcija.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
